IO-14: reject culvert codes above 57

link_readXsectParams() only rejected negative culvert codes. A code above 57
(the last entry of the culvert table) was stored; culvert_getInflow() then
ignores it, but dwflow.c has already taken the culvert branch for any code
> 0 and skipped the normal-flow limitation, so a mistyped code changed the
hydraulics without a message. Reject codes outside 0 - 57 as invalid input.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-14_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/link.c b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
index 31925e1..bc14cd4 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/link.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
@@ -262,7 +262,8 @@ int link_readXsectParams(char* tok[], int ntoks)
         if ( Link[j].type == CONDUIT && ntoks >= 8 )
         {
             i = atoi(tok[7]);
-            if ( i < 0 ) return error_setInpError(ERR_NUMBER, tok[7]);
+            if ( i < 0 || i > 57 )               // culvert codes are 1 - 57
+                return error_setInpError(ERR_NUMBER, tok[7]);
             else Link[j].xsect.culvertCode = i;
         }
     }
